implementationPlan.description:
Adversarial self-review of the three-file diff (skill adversarial-self-review), before complete_task. Check that:
- (a) every refusal precedes state.pinMessage / unpinMessage: no refused call writes a pins file, emits PINS_UPDATED or appends PIN_CREATED;
- (b) 'system' is refused before the registry lookup (otherwise it gets INVALID_INPUT, not NOT_ALLOWED), and 'human' still skips the lookup;
- (c) both tools hand the store channel.id, never params.channel;
- (d) an ambiguous name (two channels share it) resolves to null and is refused NOT_FOUND, as chat_send does;
- (e) the response shapes stay { success: true, pin } and { success: true }, and canonical ids still work (p3, p7);
- (f) no added line contains a project.json globalRails.forbiddenPatterns string;
- (g) the diff stays inside the three files, at about +142/-7 lines.

Optional mutation spot-check, run in a snapshot only, never in the worktree: /mnt/d/moe-scratch/plan-3064fd45/README.txt lists 8 clause mutants and the test case each one must kill.
